      "body": "## Claude Code Review\n\nThis pull request is from a fork — automated review is disabled. A repository maintainer can comment `@claude review` to run a one-time review.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49093#pullrequestreview-4730850401",
      "id": 4730850401,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-07-19T13:44:31Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "claude[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Confirmed on an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (SM120, capability 120, flashinfer 0.6.12): `flashinfer.mm_fp4(..., backend=\"trtllm\")` raises `BackendSupportedError: mm_fp4 does not support backend 'trtllm' with capability 120`, so the current `has_flashinfer()`-only `is_supported` does advertise a path that cannot run here.\n\nAs a control, cutlass / cudnn / b12x all get past the capability gate on the same device and only fail later on my deliberately-dummy layouts, so the rejection is trtllm-specific rather than a blanket SM120 failure. Gating on `is_device_capability_family(100)` looks right to me.\n",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49093#pullrequestreview-4732610116",
      "id": 4732610116,
      "state": "APPROVED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-07-20T06:36:01Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "waynehacking8"
      }
    }
  ]
